# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 191-197 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 16 — CHAPTERS 19-21, LEAN, 2026-09-24): the priest's conditions at the frontier (191); the
# variant piska — R. Yohanan b. Zakkai's mercy on the fearful, the brothers not enemies with Judges 21 and 2 Chronicles 28, the four fears against the four
# noises, the victory of the Omnipresent (192); the One of the wilderness, snakes and scorpions, the priest anointed for war speaks to 20:5, the widow and the
# levirate wife, the returners supply water (193); built, inherited, bought, given; sheds and silos, not gate-houses; the robber; the priest's words; "another"
# a stranger (194); planted, five trees, the four and the five, the layered and the grafted (195); the virgin and the widow, the unfit marriages (196); the very
# words, the hidden transgression, R. Akiva and R. Yose the Galilean, all return for one (197). Every row READ WHOLE; the cuts by ch19_ink.SP_. Sitting 15's form.
from ch19_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(191, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN YOU DRAW NEAR TO THE BATTLE" (20:2) — MIGHT THIS BE THE DAY THEY DRAW NEAR TO BATTLE? WHEN IT SAYS "HEAR, ISRAEL, YOU DRAW NEAR TODAY TO THE BATTLE" (20:3) THE DAY IS SAID; SO WHAT IS "WHEN YOU DRAW NEAR"? WHEN THEY REACH THE FRONTIER THE PRIEST STIPULATES WITH THEM ALL THESE CONDITIONS AND SAYS "HEAR, ISRAEL". ({SP_(191, 1, "כיון", "שמגיעים", "לספר")} "when they reach the frontier"; {SP_(191, 1, "כהן", "מתנה", "עמהם", "כל", "התנאים", "האלו")} "the priest stipulates with them all these conditions"): THE TWO SPEECHES\' TIMES — at the frontier the conditions (the exemptions), on the battle day "Hear, Israel" (Sotah 8:1 the answer sheet; the Tosefta the English\'s note) — the compile\'s two events in the war daemon. Fresh.')
srow(192, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHO IS THE MAN FEARFUL AND FAINT OF HEART … AND THE OFFICERS SHALL ADD" (20:8) — WHY ALL THESE WORDS? THAT THE CITIES OF ISRAEL BE NOT DESOLATE — RABBAN YOHANAN B. ZAKKAI\'S WORDS; SEE HOW THE OMNIPRESENT SPARED THE CREATURES\' HONOR: FOR THE FEARFUL, WHEN HE RETURNS THEY SAY "PERHAPS HE BUILT A HOUSE, PLANTED A VINEYARD, BETROTHED A WOMAN"; ALL NEED TO BRING PROOF EXCEPT THE FEARFUL, WHOSE WITNESSES ARE WITH HIM — HE HEARS THE SHIELDS CLASH AND IS TERRIFIED, THE HORSES NEIGH AND TREMBLES, THE HORNS AND IS FRIGHTENED, SEES SWORDS DRAWN AND WATER RUNS BETWEEN HIS KNEES. The variant piska\'s first row, heading on 20:8 out of verse order ({SP_(192, 1, "שלא", "יהו", "ערי", "ישראל", "נשמות")} "that the cities of Israel be not desolate"; {SP_(192, 1, "שעדיו", "עמו")} "whose witnesses are with him"): R. Yohanan b. Zakkai\'s REASON for the three exemptions before the fourth — the fearful man\'s shame covered (Sotah 8:5 the English\'s note; the material unevenly attested); the compile\'s note: the exemptions need PROOF (a parameter) except the fearful. Fresh.')
srow(192, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "HEAR, ISRAEL, YOU DRAW NEAR TODAY TO BATTLE AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" (20:3) — AND NOT AGAINST YOUR BROTHERS: NOT JUDAH AGAINST SIMEON NOR SIMEON AGAINST JUDAH, WHO WOULD HAVE MERCY IF YOU FELL INTO THEIR HAND, AS AT BENJAMIN (JUDGES 21:3) AND AT ODED\'S WORD (2 CHRONICLES 28:8-15) — AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES YOU GO, WHO WILL NOT PITY YOU. ({SP_(192, 2, "ולא", "על", "אחיכם")} "and not against your brothers"; {SP_(192, 2, "לא", "יהודה", "על", "שמעון")} "not Judah against Simeon"): "YOUR ENEMIES" NOT YOUR BROTHERS (Sotah 8:1 the answer sheet) — the two Prophets\' and Writings\' cases the run\'s (never read ahead: rows in the spine, not the tape) — the compile\'s enemy parameter excludes Israel. Fresh.')
srow(192, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET NOT YOUR HEART FAINT, FEAR NOT, TREMBLE NOT, DREAD NOT BEFORE THEM" — THE HEART FOR THE HORSES\' NEIGHING, "FEAR NOT" FOR THE SHIELDS\' CLASH AND THE BOOTS\' TRAMP, "TREMBLE NOT" FOR THE HORNS\' SOUND, "DREAD NOT" FOR THE SHOUTING — AGAINST FOUR THINGS THE NATIONS DO: CLASH, BLOW, SHOUT, TRAMPLE. "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD GOES WITH YOU" — THEY COME IN THE VICTORY OF FLESH AND BLOOD, YOU IN THE VICTORY OF THE OMNIPRESENT. ({SP_(192, 3, "כנגד", "ארבעה", "דברים", "שאמות", "העולם", "עושים")} "against four things the nations of the world do"; {SP_(192, 3, "בנצחונו", "של", "מקום")} "in the victory of the Omnipresent"): THE FOUR FEARS MAPPED TO FOUR NOISES (Sotah 8:1) — the priest\'s speech a table of four; the compile\'s parameter set. Fresh.')
srow(193, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD GOES WITH YOU" (20:4) — HE WHO WAS WITH YOU IN THE WILDERNESS WILL BE WITH YOU IN THE TIME OF TROUBLE; "THE LORD WILL FIGHT FOR YOU AND YOU SHALL BE SILENT" (EXODUS 14:14). ({SP_(193, 1, "מי", "שהיה", "עמכם", "במדבר")} "He who was with you in the wilderness"): the Sea\'s promise the priest\'s ground (190:21\'s Egypt; 1:30\'s "who goes before you" the kin) — the compile\'s reference row to the tape\'s Exodus 14 line. Fresh.')
srow(193, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"TO FIGHT FOR YOU WITH YOUR ENEMIES, TO SAVE YOU" — FROM SERPENTS AND SCORPIONS AND EVIL SPIRITS. ({SP_(193, 2, "משרפים", "ועקרבים", "ורוחות", "הרעים")} "from serpents and scorpions and evil spirits"): the salvation widened past the enemy — no rule. Fresh.')
srow(193, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE OFFICERS SHALL SPEAK" (20:5) — UP TO HERE THE PRIEST ANOINTED FOR WAR SPEAKS; FROM HERE ON, "AND THE OFFICERS SHALL SPEAK". ({SP_(193, 3, "עד", "כאן", "משוח", "מלחמה", "מדבר")} "up to here the one anointed for war speaks"): THE SPEAKERS DIVIDED AT 20:5 — the priest anointed for war (Sotah 8:1 names him; the anointing a status the compile installs) to 20:4, the officers from 20:5 — the compile\'s two speaker roles. Fresh.')
srow(193, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO HAS BETROTHED A WOMAN" (20:7) — EVEN A WIDOW, EVEN ONE AWAITING THE LEVIR, EVEN ONE WHO HEARD HIS BROTHER DIED IN THE WAR — HE RETURNS. ({SP_(193, 4, "אפלו", "אלמנה")} "even a widow"; {SP_(193, 4, "אפלו", "שומרת", "יבם")} "even one awaiting the levir"): the betrothal exemption\'s persons (196:1 the same, whole) — the levirate wife inside it (25:5 ahead) — the compile\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(193, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL GO AND RETURN TO HIS HOUSE" — ALL HEAR THE PRIEST\'S WORDS FROM THE BATTLE LINES AND RETURN, AND SUPPLY WATER AND FOOD TO THEIR BROTHERS AND REPAIR THE ROADS. ({SP_(193, 5, "ומספקים", "מים", "ומזון", "לאחיהם")} "and supply water and food to their brothers"; {SP_(193, 5, "ומתקנים", "את", "הדרכים")} "and repair the roads"): THE RETURNERS\' DUTY — not home but the supply line (Sotah 8:2 the answer sheet; the smaller type the English\'s note) — the compile\'s exempt status carries a service. Fresh.')
srow(193, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE OFFICERS SHALL SPEAK" — MIGHT THEY SPEAK OTHER WORDS? WHEN IT SAYS "AND THE OFFICERS SHALL ADD TO SPEAK TO THE PEOPLE" (20:8) THESE ARE THE WORDS; WHY "AND THE OFFICERS SHALL SPEAK"? WHEN THE OFFICER BEGINS TO SPEAK THE PRIEST MAKES THEM HEAR THESE CONDITIONS. ({SP_(193, 6, "כיון", "שהתחיל", "שוטר", "לדבר")} "when the officer began to speak"): the officer opens, the priest voices — the sequence of the two roles (Sotah 8:1-3 the answer sheet\'s "the priest speaks and the officer proclaims") — the compile\'s speech order. Fresh.')
srow(194, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO IS THE MAN WHO HAS BUILT" (20:5) — I HAVE ONLY BUILT; INHERITED, BOUGHT, GIVEN AS A GIFT? "WHO IS THE MAN WHO HAS BUILT". ({SP_(194, 1, "ירש", "לקח", "נתן", "לו", "במתנה", "מנין")} "inherited, bought, given to him as a gift — whence?"): THE HOUSE\'S ACQUISITION ANY (Sotah 8:2 the answer sheet) — the compile\'s exemption keyed on possession, not the act of building. Fresh.')
srow(194, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"A HOUSE" — I HAVE ONLY A HOUSE; A STRAW-SHED, A CATTLE-SHED, A WOOD-SHED, A STOREHOUSE? "WHO HAS BUILT". MIGHT IT BE EVEN A GATE-HOUSE, A PORTICO, A BALCONY? "A HOUSE" — AS A HOUSE IS A DWELLING, THESE ARE EXCLUDED. ({SP_(194, 2, "בית", "התבן", "ובית", "הבקר")} "the straw-shed and the cattle-shed"; {SP_(194, 2, "בית", "שער", "אכסדרה", "ומרפסת")} "a gate-house, a portico and a balcony"; {SP_(194, 2, "שהוא", "בית", "דירה")} "that it is a dwelling house"): THE HOUSE\'S CLASS — a dwelling of any use, not a passage (Sotah 8:2-3) — the compile\'s parameter (the dwelling test). Fresh.')
srow(194, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAS NOT DEDICATED IT" — TO EXCLUDE THE ROBBER. ({SP_(194, 3, "פרט", "לגזלן")} "to exclude the robber"): the stolen house no exemption — the compile\'s condition (lawful possession). Fresh.')
srow(194, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL GO AND RETURN TO HIS HOUSE" — HE GOES AND HEARS THE PRIEST\'S WORDS FROM THE BATTLE LINES AND RETURNS. ({SP_(194, 4, "וישמע", "דברי", "כהן")} "and hears the priest\'s words"): the exempt man hears the speech first, then goes (193:5 the duty after) — the order of events. Fresh.')
srow(194, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST HE DIE IN THE BATTLE" — IF HE DOES NOT HEED THE PRIEST\'S WORDS, IN THE END HE DIES IN THE BATTLE. ({SP_(194, 5, "לסוף", "הוא", "מת", "במלחמה")} "in the end he dies in the battle"): "lest" read as the SANCTION of disobedience (195:6 the same) — the compile\'s effect on the one who stays. Fresh.')
srow(194, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ANOTHER MAN DEDICATE IT" — MIGHT IT BE HIS UNCLE OR HIS COUSIN? "ANOTHER" IS SAID HERE AND "ANOTHER" THERE (20:7): AS THERE A STRANGER, SO HERE A STRANGER. ({SP_(194, 6, "יכול", "דודו", "ובן", "דודו")} "might it be his uncle or his cousin?"; {SP_(194, 6, "נכרי")} "a stranger"): "ANOTHER" = a stranger by the gezerah shavah (the analogy of equal words) with 20:7 (28:30\'s curse the English\'s note) — the compile\'s note on the exemption\'s ground (the loss to a stranger). Fresh.')
srow(195, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHO IS THE MAN WHO HAS PLANTED" (20:6) — I HAVE ONLY PLANTED; INHERITED, BOUGHT, GIVEN? "WHO IS THE MAN WHO HAS PLANTED". ({SP_(195, 1, "ירש", "לקח", "נתן", "לו", "במתנה", "מנין")} "inherited, bought, given to him as a gift — whence?"): the vineyard\'s acquisition any (194:1\'s form) — Sotah 8:2. Fresh.')
srow(195, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"A VINEYARD" — I HAVE ONLY A VINEYARD; ONE WHO PLANTS FIVE FRUIT TREES, EVEN OF FIVE KINDS? "WHO HAS PLANTED". MIGHT IT BE EVEN FOUR FRUIT TREES OR FIVE BARREN TREES? "A VINEYARD". ({SP_(195, 2, "חמשה", "אילני", "מאכל")} "five fruit trees"; {SP_(195, 2, "ארבעה", "אילני", "מאכל", "וחמשה", "אילני", "סרק")} "four fruit trees and five barren trees"): THE VINEYARD\'S THRESHOLD — five fruit trees (Sotah 8:2; the vineyard\'s definition Kilayim 4-5 the count), four not, barren not — the compile\'s parameter (five fruit trees). Fresh.')
srow(195, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER B. JACOB: I HEAR ONLY A VINEYARD. ({SP_(195, 3, "אין", "לי", "במשמע", "אלא", "כרם")} "I have in the sense only a vineyard"): the dissent — a vineyard literal (the row with no verse citation in either file); the compile keeps the dispute (five trees / a vineyard). Fresh.')
srow(195, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAS NOT REDEEMED IT" — TO EXCLUDE THE LAYERER; "AND HAS NOT REDEEMED IT" — TO EXCLUDE THE GRAFTER. ({SP_(195, 4, "פרט", "למבריך")} "to exclude the layerer"; {SP_(195, 4, "פרט", "למרכיב")} "to exclude the grafter"): THE FOURTH YEAR\'S REDEMPTION (Leviticus 19:23-25 — "profane it" the fourth-year fruit\'s release) presupposed: a layered or grafted vine is not "planted" for the exemption (Sotah 8:2) — the compile\'s condition and its cross-call to the orlah clock. Fresh.')
srow(195, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL GO AND RETURN TO HIS HOUSE" — HE GOES AND HEARS THE PRIEST\'S WORDS FROM THE BATTLE LINES AND RETURNS. ({SP_(195, 5, "וישמע", "דברי", "כהן")} "and hears the priest\'s words"): 194:4\'s row at the vineyard. Fresh.')
srow(195, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST HE DIE IN THE BATTLE" — IF HE DOES NOT HEED THE PRIEST\'S WORDS, IN THE END HE DIES IN THE BATTLE. ({SP_(195, 6, "לסוף", "הוא", "מת", "במלחמה")} "in the end he dies in the battle"): 194:5\'s row at the vineyard. Fresh.')
srow(195, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ANOTHER MAN REDEEM IT" — HIS UNCLE OR COUSIN? "ANOTHER" HERE AND "ANOTHER" THERE (20:7): A STRANGER. ({SP_(195, 7, "יכול", "דודו", "ובן", "דודו")} "might it be his uncle or his cousin?"): 194:6\'s analogy at the vineyard. Fresh.')
srow(196, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHO IS THE MAN WHO HAS BETROTHED A WOMAN" (20:7) — THE ONE WHO BETROTHS A VIRGIN AND THE ONE WHO BETROTHS A WIDOW, EVEN ONE AWAITING THE LEVIR, EVEN ONE WHO HEARD HIS BROTHER DIED IN THE WAR — HE RETURNS AND COMES. ({SP_(196, 1, "אחד", "המארס", "את", "הבתולה")} "the one who betroths the virgin"; {SP_(196, 1, "ואפלו", "שומרת", "יבם")} "and even one awaiting the levir"): 193:4 whole at its own head (Sotah 8:2) — the persons of the third exemption. Fresh.')
srow(196, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HAS NOT TAKEN HER" — A WOMAN FIT FOR HIM; TO EXCLUDE ONE WHO REMARRIES HIS DIVORCEE, A WIDOW TO A HIGH PRIEST, A DIVORCEE OR A RELEASED WIDOW TO A COMMON PRIEST, A MAMZERET OR A NETINAH TO AN ISRAELITE, AN ISRAELITE\'S DAUGHTER TO A NATIN OR A MAMZER. ({SP_(196, 2, "באשה", "הראויה", "לו")} "a woman fit for him"; {SP_(196, 2, "ואלמנה", "לכהן", "גדול")} "and a widow to a high priest"; {SP_(196, 2, "ממזרת", "ונתינה", "לישראל")} "a mamzeret (impaired lineage) or a netinah (Gibeonite) to an Israelite"): THE FORBIDDEN MARRIAGES NO EXEMPTION (Sotah 8:3 the answer sheet; the lineage classes of Kiddushin 4 — the priesthood\'s bars Leviticus 21:7, 14) — the compile\'s condition (a lawful betrothal). Fresh.')
srow(196, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE SHALL GO AND RETURN TO HIS HOUSE" — HE GOES AND HEARS THE PRIEST\'S WORDS FROM THE BATTLE LINES AND RETURNS. ({SP_(196, 3, "וישמע", "דברי", "כהן")} "and hears the priest\'s words"): the third exemption\'s order (Sotah 8:3). Fresh.')
srow(197, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE OFFICERS SHALL ADD TO SPEAK TO THE PEOPLE AND SAY" (20:8) — WE LEARNED THAT THESE ARE THE WORDS. ({SP_(197, 1, "למדנו", "שהם", "הדברים")} "we learned that these are the words"): the fourth speech the officers\' own words (193:6) — the speaker of 20:8 the officer alone. Fresh.')
srow(197, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO IS THE MAN FEARFUL AND FAINT OF HEART" — ONE WHO HAS A TRANSGRESSION IN HIS HAND IN SECRET; "HE SHALL GO AND RETURN TO HIS HOUSE". ({SP_(197, 2, "שיש", "עברה", "בידו", "בסתר")} "who has a transgression in his hand in secret"): THE FEARFUL = THE SECRET SINNER (Sotah 8:5 — R. Yose the Galilean\'s view in the Mishnah) — the fourth exemption keyed on a hidden transgression; the compile\'s parameter (a status the ledger does not see — the readback\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(197, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: "FEARFUL AND FAINT OF HEART" AS IT SOUNDS. R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: FEARFUL AND FAINT OF HEART — ONE WITH A BLEMISH. ({SP_(197, 3, "כמשמעו")} "as it sounds"; {SP_(197, 3, "שהוא", "בעל", "מום")} "that he has a blemish"): THE THREE READINGS OF THE FEARFUL — literal (R. Akiva), the sinner (197:2), the blemished (R. Yose the Galilean here; 190:16\'s whole soldier) — Sotah 8:5\'s dispute the exam row (the row with no verse citation in either file). Fresh.')
srow(197, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HE MELT NOT HIS BROTHERS\' HEART LIKE HIS HEART" — IF ONE OF THEM FEARED THE TRANSGRESSIONS IN HIS HAND, ALL RETURN AND COME. ({SP_(197, 4, "כלם", "חוזרים", "ובאים")} "all return and come"): the fearful\'s return COVERED by the others\' — the three exemptions the cover for the fourth (192:1\'s reason; Sotah 8:5 the English\'s note names 5:8 — read whole, the number the export\'s) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
